1. **A method for controlling a user interface, comprising:**  
   receiving, from a force sensor, force measurements indicative of a force applied by a user to an input surface;  
   comparing the force measurements with a force threshold;  
   in response to determining that the force satisfies the force threshold, initiating a timer;  
   activating a menu-scrolling operation when the force continues to satisfy the force threshold for at least a predetermined activation interval;  
   during the menu-scrolling operation, causing a haptic output device to generate one or more pressure waves perceptible by the user; and  
   repeatedly advancing through menu items at a scroll frequency that varies in proportion to a magnitude of the measured force.
